ist_reservations", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Dana Lee's flight and hotel are both booked and confirmed. They ended up as two separate bookings instead of one combined trip.\n\n- **Flight (R0001):** F100, the cheapest nonstop from SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, for $289. A cheaper flight at $199 has a stop, so I didn't pick it.\n- **Hotel (R0002):** Midtown Lodge, $189/night, 2 nights checking in 2026-11-12, for $378. This was the cheapest New York hotel under $250/night.\n- **Total charged to the corporate card:** $667. That's under the $1,000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\n**What happened:** The combined booking timed out. When I retried it, the system said the first attempt had partly failed: the flight was booked but the hotel wasn't. I checked Dana's reservations to confirm that, then booked only the hotel separately. The final check shows exactly one confirmed flight and one confirmed hotel, with no duplicate charges.", "type": "text"}]}]}